# The frozen integrity zome.
#
# A circle IS the hash of this compiled wasm. Change the source — including a
# comment, which was measured to change it — and every circle anybody has ever
# made becomes unreachable. Their records stay on their own disks and no build
# of this app will ever show them again, with no error anywhere.
#
# So the hash is pinned here and CI fails if it moves. See the README, and
# docs/to-a-product.md for what to do if it genuinely has to change (short
# answer: that is a migration with everybody re-invited, not a commit).
#
# Rebased 2026-09-09, when the build stopped embedding the building machine's
# home directory. Frozen from the release that follows.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build it with scripts/build-zomes.mjs, never with cargo directly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rust bakes the source path of every dependency into the binary for its panic
# messages. A bare `cargo build` therefore produces a different hash on every
# computer — and the installer released on 2026-09-08 carried the string
# `C:\Users\user\...` inside it. The wrapper passes --remap-path-prefix so that
# any machine of the same platform now produces the same bytes.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows and Linux still differ, and no flag on stable Rust fixes it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The remapped paths keep the operating system's own separator:
#
#   Windows  /cargo\registry\src\...
#   Linux    /cargo/registry/src/...
#
# Different bytes, different DNA, different network. So the two lines below are
# not a reproducibility failure to be fixed — they are a fact about the
# toolchain, and the reason **the released .webhapp is the canonical build**.
# Anybody making a desktop app for another platform assembles it from that
# file rather than compiling the zomes. See the README.

linux    UNKNOWN-until-the-first-CI-run
windows  392dc1703ce4e2a381082784cb9c0169065dd9dff680f90c42679ae0e88b29df
